# Composing Stores

Stores can use other stores, enabling you to compose complex logic.

```javascript
export const useUserStore = defineStore('user', () => {
  const cartStore = useCartStore();

  function buy() {
    // use cartStore
  }

  return { buy };
})
```

This creates a dependency tree that works seamlessly.

# Extending Pinia with Plugins

Plugins allow you to add global features to all stores, like persisting state to localStorage.

```javascript
const pinia = createPinia()

pinia.use(({ store }) => {
  // Called for every store
  store.$subscribe((mutation, state) => {
    localStorage.setItem(store.$id, JSON.stringify(state))
  })
})
```

Popular plugins: `pinia-plugin-persistedstate`.
